is\n$intA = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: 0 < x < 1, A A A A A}$.\nWhat is the missing expression?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1" :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6d1de36-c45f-576e-a7f1-ddd4556e6e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4\\cos θ, y = 49\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149130} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e6c06b-fbd2-58df-8e45-287b8f1bd672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\sin θ, y = 7\\cos θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149131} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f202dd-0ca4-50e2-93ae-12d42b873745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7\\cos θ, y = 2\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149132} {:answer/id #uuid "bebafa99-24a7-5707-8536-24d126c9d58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7\\sin θ, y = 2\\cos θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149133} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9a2b8e-346c-559b-aa35-5c942ebd9ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2\\cos θ, y = 7\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149134}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d808a2-555f-5182-9d76-592cf8cf6ea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149129}] :question/id #uuid "46c88046-0f62-50bb-8a31-ae13a6c535ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15856" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c46972a3968d7110cb08d4b16bfff9267e49b102cf005cdbb21a3630d15c49d.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $7$ and vertical radius $2$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $θ ∈ [0, 2π)$, traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(7, 0)$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "efb1958d-